  - Key idea: FM synthesis gives us a theoretically _infinite_ number of sidebands with a _finite_ at $f_c +- k \cdot f_m$
    - If we _ very carefully_ control the parameters of FM synthesis over time, we could emulate very sophisticated instrumental behavior!
  - Deriving this is beyond the scope of this course... see REF for more details
  - Rule of thumb, number of _significant_ (audible) sidebands is determined by the _index of modulation_ $I = \frac{D}{f_m}$. Namely, the number of audible sidebands is roughly $I + 1$
